   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Reporting what someone said",
     "texto": [
      "To report what someone said, use **sagde at** (said that) or **fortalte at** (told that). The sentence with **at** follows subordinate word order: the subject comes before **ikke** and **altid**: **at han ikke kunne komme**.",
      "Example: **Hun sagde, at hun var træt.** = She said she was tired."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Tense changes",
     "texto": [
      "In a narrative where the main verb is in the past, this change usually happens: present → past; past and present perfect → past perfect; **vil** → **ville**; **skal** → **skulle**; **kan** → **kunne**.",
      "Example: **Han sagde, at han ville komme.** = He said he would come. (Direct: «Jeg vil komme».) The tense also depends on when what is reported happens and whether it is still valid; don't change the tense mechanically."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Direct sentence",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Reported sentence",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
